To create a phishing simulation, follow these steps to craft a realistic and harmless phishing attack for educational purposes. This simulation will help study user responses without causing harm.

### Tools and Technologies:
- **HTML/CSS/JavaScript**: For creating the email and login pages.
- **Python/Tkinter**: For displaying the simulation in a GUI.
- **Local Data Handling**: To capture and log input data without internet access.

### Steps to Create the Phishing Simulation:

1. **Craft the Phishing Email (HTML)**
   - **Structure**: Create an email template that includes a header, body, and a link.
   - **Content**: Use placeholders for personalization, such as the user's name.
   - **Styling**: Use a professional design with a fake company logo and a sense of urgency.
   - **Subject Line**: Make it attention-grabbing, e.g., "Immediate Action Required: Security Alert."
   - **Body**: Include a message prompting the user to click a link to log in securely.
   - **Link**: Redirect to a fake login page (e.g., `https://secure-login.example.com/login`).

2. **Create the Fake Login Page (HTML)**
   - **Structure**: A clean login interface with username and password fields.
   - **Styling**: Mimic a real login page with a secure connection indicator.
   - **Form Submission**: Include a submit button that triggers a local script.
   - **Fields**: Two text inputs for username and password, and a "Sign In" button.

3. **Develop the Simulation in Python**
   - **Display the Email**: Use Tkinter to open the email as a pop-up window.
   - **Display the Login Page**: Similarly, open the login page in a separate window.
   - **Data Capture**: Use JavaScript or a Python script to capture input data.
   - **Local Logging**: Store captured data in a text file on the local system.
   - **Success Message**: Show a confirmation message upon successful input, indicating the simulation was successful.

4. **Testing and Refinement**
   - **Visual Check**: Ensure the email and login page look authentic.
   - **Functionality**: Test the submission process and data capture.
   - **Security**: Ensure no data is transmitted over the internet and is handled locally.

### Example Code:

```python
import tkinter as tk
from tkinter import messagebox

# Create the phishing email content
email_html = """
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: #f5f5f5;
        }
        .email-container {
            max-width: 600px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: white;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
        .logo {
            width: 200px;
            height: 50px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .urgent {
            color: #ff4444;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        .button {
            background-color: #007bff;
            color: white;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border-radius: 5px;
            text-decoration: none;
            display: inline-block;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }
        .button:hover {
            background-color: #0056b3;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="email-container">
        <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/200x80" alt="Logo" class="logo">
        <h2>Security Alert: Your Account is Compromised</h2>
        <p>Dear {username},</p>
        <p>Your account security is at risk. We have detected unusual activity on your account. Please click the button below to secure your account immediately:</p>
        <center>
            <a href="https://secure-login.example.com/login" class="button">Secure Your Account Now</a>
        </center>
        <p>If you did not request this email, ignore it. This is a security measure to protect your account.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
"""

# Create the login page
login_html = """
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #f0f2f5;
        }
        .login-container {
            max-width: 400px;
            margin: 100px auto;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: white;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
        h2 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #333;
        }
        .form-group {
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }
        label {
            display: block;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
            color: #666;
        }
        input {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 8px;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            border-radius: 4px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        button {
            background-color: #007bff;
            color: white;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
            width: 100%;
        }
        button:hover {
            background-color: #0056b3;
        }
        .info {
            color: #666;
            font-size: 0.9em;
            margin-top: 15px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="login-container">
        <h2>Account Login</h2>
        <form id="loginForm">
            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="username">Username or Email</label>
                <input type="text" id="username" required>
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="password">Password</label>
                <input type="password" id="password" required>
            </div>
            <button type="submit">Sign In</button>
            <div class="info">Security check required. Please ensure all information is correct.</div>
        </form>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
"""

# Create the main GUI
root = tk.Tk()
root.title("Phishing Simulation")

# Function to show the phishing email
def show_email():
    email_root = tk.Toplevel(root)
    email_root.title("Security Alert: Your Account is Compromised")
    email_root.geometry("600x800")
    email_root.config(bg="white")
    # Load the email content
    email_label = tk.Label(email_root, text=email_html, wraplength=600)
    email_label.pack()

# Function to show the login page
def show_login():
    login_root = tk.Toplevel(root)
    login_root.title("Secure Your Account")
    login_root.geometry("400x500")
    login_root.config(bg="white")
    # Load the login form
    login_form = tk.Frame(login_root)
    login_form.pack()

    # Variables to store captured data
    username = tk.StringVar()
    password = tk.StringVar()

    # Widgets
    username_label = tk.Label(login_form, text="Username or Email")
    username_label.pack(anchor='w')

    username_entry = tk.Entry(login_form, textvariable=username)
    username_entry.pack()

    password_label = tk.Label(login_form, text="Password")
    password_label.pack(anchor='w')

    password_entry = tk.Entry(login_form, textvariable=password, show='*')
    password_entry.pack()

    submit_button = tk.Button(login_form, text="Sign In", command=lambda: submit())
    submit_button.pack()

    # Function to capture data and log
    def submit():
        data = f"Username: {username.get()}\nPassword: {password.get()}\n\n"
        with open("phishing_data.txt", "a") as f:
            f.write(data)
        # Show success message
        messagebox.showinfo("Success", "Phishing attempt recorded.")
        login_root.destroy()

    # Close the window
    login_root.protocol("WM_DELETE WINDOW", lambda: login_root.destroy())

# Start the simulation
root.geometry("500x300")
root.callbak= lambda: root.destroy()  # To close the main window after 5 seconds
root.after(5000, root.destroy)  # Auto-close after 5 seconds

# Buttons to trigger the simulation
button_submit = tk.Button(root, text="Open Phishing Attack", command=show_email)
button_submit.pack(pady=20)

# Run the application
root.mainloop()
```

### Explanation:
1. **Email Simulation**: The phishing email is displayed in a new window, prompting users to click a link to "Secure Your Account."
2. **Login Page**: Upon clicking the link, the login page appears, capturing username and password inputs.
3. **Data Capture**: The entered credentials are saved in a text file on the local system.
4. **Non-Harmful**: The simulation doesn't send data over the internet and doesn't install malware.
5. **Educational Use**: This tool is designed for research and education to understand user behavior without causing harm.<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>

